0.12 0.34 0.55 RG 50 730 m 545 730 l S
0.08 0.20 0.35 rg BT /F2 14 Tf 50 637 Td (Sequential circuits) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 615 Td (The sequential RTL includes a D flip-flop, an 8-bit register, and a shift register.) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 600 Td (Synchronous reset is sampled on the active clock edge. Asynchronous reset acts) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 585 Td (independently of that edge. Edge-triggered state updates use nonblocking assignments.) Tj ET
0.08 0.20 0.35 rg BT /F2 14 Tf 50 562 Td (Counters and parameterized blocks) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 540 Td (Implemented counters: 4-bit up and down, Mod-10, 4-bit ring, and 4-bit Johnson.) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 525 Td (Parameterized register, counter, and shift-register modules support multiple widths.) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 510 Td (The self-checking parameter testbench exercises both 4-bit and 8-bit instances.) Tj ET
0.08 0.20 0.35 rg BT /F2 14 Tf 50 487 Td (Finite state machines) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 465 Td (Traffic-light examples include a Moore controller and a Mealy controller with an) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 450 Td (emergency input. The vending machine accepts 5-unit and 10-unit coins for a 15-unit) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 435 Td (product. The elevator controller handles requests among three floors.) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 420 Td (The mini-project is an autonomous Moore traffic-light controller with configurable) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 405 Td (RED, GREEN, and YELLOW durations. Its outputs depend on the registered state.) Tj ET
0.08 0.20 0.35 rg BT /F2 14 Tf 50 382 Td (Design documentation) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 360 Td (SVG diagrams show the RTL overview, traffic-light FSM, vending FSM, elevator FSM,) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 345 Td (and a conceptual clock/reset timing illustration. Counter sequences and reset behavior) Tj ET
0.12 0.16 0.20 rg BT /F1 10 Tf 50 330 Td (are described in docs/design_notes.md.) Tj ET
